<title>AUSTRALIA: No comment on Australia's media rules - Alston.</title>
<headline>No comment on Australia's media rules - Alston.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Communications Minister Richard Alston declined on Thursday to comment on reports the government planned to ease media ownership rules.</p>
<p>&quot;I'm not confirming or denying anything,&quot; Alston told reporters. Alston said the government was still considering the issue and would announce its decision when appropriate.</p>
<p>&quot;We'll do it in the fullness of time,&quot; he said, when asked when the decision would be made.  </p>
<p>Newspapers on Thursday reported that tough media ownership limits may be eased, allowing media tycoons Kerry Packer and Rupert Murdoch to expand their empires and foreigners to take bigger media stakes.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
